WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.437
The federal requirement.

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:06.379
This gate supports NIST special publication
eight hundred fifty-three A C two,

3
00:00:06.379 --> 00:00:09.876
enhancement one, automated
system account management.

4
00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:14.730
It supports I A five: the initial
authenticator is time-limited, and goes to

5
00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:19.425
an accountable person; that's the short,
one-time pass sent to the manager.

6
00:00:19.425 --> 00:00:25.437
And it supports O M B M-22-09's
phishing-resistant multifactor authentication,

7
00:00:25.437 --> 00:00:30.087
which the Temporary Access Pass
bridges to until the PIV card is bound.

8
00:00:30.087 --> 00:00:34.262
Your organization still sets the
organization-defined parameters,

9
00:00:34.262 --> 00:00:37.412
and the assessor decides
whether each is satisfied.

10
00:00:37.412 --> 00:00:42.298
The evidence an ISSO keeps for Gate
3: the reviewed workflow files,

11
00:00:42.298 --> 00:00:46.550
and the plan that changed each
version, with its manifest.

12
00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:49.924
The lint's clean run, showing
a one-time pass of at most

13
00:00:49.924 --> 00:00:54.475
twenty-four hours and an execution
limit on every scheduled workflow.

14
00:00:54.475 --> 00:00:56.962
The readiness summary for each start date.

15
00:00:56.962 --> 00:01:01.660
And the workflows' run history,
exported past Entra's thirty-day view.
